00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:36.740
So a good place to start
is with Kubernetes.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:39.170
Kubernetes is an
open source project,

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:41.000
a container centric
infrastructure

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:44.760
founded by Google at 2014.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:47.270
It's based on all of
our years of experience

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:49.460
running containers.

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:52.700
When we started with
Google Cloud Platform,

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:54.800
we thought to ourself,
should we provide

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.490
something similar to
what we have internally

00:03:57.490 --> 00:04:01.280
to run our own
containers to our users?

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:04.280
The obvious answer
was yes, but the team

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:07.020
insisted it will be open source.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:09.900
You can imagine it
was a hard to preach

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:12.870
to make to take something
that differentiated us,

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:17.709
until that day, and make it open
source, available to everybody.

00:04:17.709 --> 00:04:20.450
So why open source?

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:23.970
First of all, as developers,
we all powerful open source.

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:27.270
We lack the credibility
knowing what inside,

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:30.020
how the code looks like,
knowing the developers,

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.395
having visibility
to the roadmap.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:36.710
It also provides us flexibility.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:40.240
So if you would like to change
things that will meet our need,

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:41.230
we are able to do that.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:43.285
We can integrate
different types of tools.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:48.950
And for us as an
engineering team,

00:04:48.950 --> 00:04:51.860
we needed that
immediate feedback loop.

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:53.810
So we knew how we are
running production,

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:57.570
and we knew how we are
running Google applications,

00:04:57.570 --> 00:04:59.720
but we didn't know
much about how

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:04.080
everybody else are doing that,
and that was really important.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.830
So by building a community
around our open source project,

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:10.130
we were able to get feedback
from partners, customers,

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:14.290
and just individual
contributors.

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:17.570
And we have taken it seriously,
and we have donated Kubernetes

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:19.850
to the Cloud Native
Compute Foundation,

00:05:19.850 --> 00:05:21.650
and we are also
building programs

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:26.120
to help users make informed
decisions with whom

00:05:26.120 --> 00:05:27.620
they should partner
and where they

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:30.140
should put their workloads.

00:05:30.140 --> 00:05:32.810
Managing a community
takes a lot of effort

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.670
and we invest a lot in that.

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:36.960
So as much as we invest
in the technology,

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:40.340
we also invest in helping
partners and users, wherever

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:44.760
they are, use and
leverage Kubernetes.

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:46.951
And I think we're doing
a good job at that.

00:05:46.951 --> 00:05:48.450
Looking at the
Kubernetes community,

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.270
you can see a lot of names.

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:56.520
Some of them are speaking in
this conference, Sam from Box.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:58.580
And what I like
about this community

00:05:58.580 --> 00:06:01.710
that not only
people are adopting,

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:04.200
both contributors,
both vendors, and users

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:06.930
are contributing back.

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:10.080
So if Kubernetes is so amazing,
its an open source technology

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:12.000
and everybody can
use it, then why

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.490
do you need Google
Container Engine?

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:17.580
So first of all, yes,
it is still Kubernetes,

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:19.430
and we are very proud of that.

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:22.710
Kubernetes is a very good tool
to automate the deployment,

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:27.030
and scheduling, and management
of containerized applications.

00:06:27.030 --> 00:06:29.760
On top of that, we are bringing
our own experience, [INAUDIBLE]

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:33.540
of experience to manage
your cloud still,

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:35.580
and we do all of that
on top of Google Cloud

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:38.850
Platform with the best
network, persistent disk,

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:42.360
amazing performance, and
such features on Google Cloud

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:43.770
Platform.

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:46.410
This provides for
you, the best platform

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:48.330
to manage your
applications, instead

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:50.801
of focusing on the machine
and the infrastructure.

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:57.380
And of course,
running in production

00:06:57.380 --> 00:07:00.140
means worldwide at scale.

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.944
You can see this is
our current regions,

00:07:01.944 --> 00:07:03.360
and of course, the
future regions.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:06.125
So we keep expanding the reach
of Google Cloud Platform.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:10.720
So how can I convince
you that this is ready

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:14.560
and the technology is ready to
run your production workloads?

00:07:14.560 --> 00:07:17.590
I think the best way to do it
is just to use by real customer

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:19.870
examples.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:21.400
Niantic was a big story for us.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:24.220
Very exciting last year.

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:25.810
They chose Google
Container Engine

00:07:25.810 --> 00:07:27.940
for its ability to
orchestrate their containers

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:31.042
